+
+Actual execution evidence is mandatory for all qualified adapter admission, including dry-run validation. The referenced immutable record must match the selected validator/source, native process, Identity results, reset and reset-check results; reset/audit records retain their hash/process/chronology bindings. Original legacy receipts remain untouched and cannot provide a qualified adapter under this contract.
+
+Descriptor qualifiedAt must be a finite string timestamp, at or after the mock qualification and no later than the actual current same-host clock (zero future tolerance). An explicitly supplied descriptor expiry must be finite and unexpired. These checks repeat before every forwarded request; no implicit TTL or new qualification date is invented for an older live mock. Expected root grant/action set and author pins are frozen in producer code; those values and hashes identify a registered task binding, not a signature or human-approval proof.
